{"name":"Graphite","hex":"#383428","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"graphite","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An allotrope of carbon, consisting of planes of carbon atoms arranged in hexagonal arrays with the planes stacked loosely, that is used as a dry lubricant, in \"lead\" pencils, and as a moderator in some nuclear reactors.","Graphite-reinforced plastic, a composite plastic made with graphite fibers noted for lightweight strength and stiffness."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To apply graphite to."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/graphite"}],"entries":[{"title":"Graphite","blocks":[{"text":"Graphite is a crystalline allotrope (form) of the element carbon. It consists of many stacked layers of graphene, typically in excess of hundreds of layers. Graphite occurs naturally and is the most stable form of carbon under standard conditions. Synthetic and natural graphite are consumed on a large scale for uses in many critical industries including refractories (50%), lithium-ion batteries (18%), foundries (10%), and lubricants (5%), among others (17%). Graphite converts to diamond under extremely high pressure and temperature. Graphite's low cost, thermal and chemical inertness and characteristic conductivity of heat and electricity finds numerous applications in high energy and high temperature processes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Graphite-233436.jpg/330px-Graphite-233436.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Graphite","wikidata":"Q5309"},{"title":"Graphite (smart font technology)","blocks":[{"text":"Graphite is a programmable Unicode-compliant smart font technology and rendering system developed by SIL International as free software, distributed under the terms of the GNU Lesser General Public License and the Common Public License."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Graphite_(smart_font_technology)","wikidata":"Q1027984"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Graphite_found_near_Mautern.jpg/500px-Graphite_found_near_Mautern.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Graphite_found_near_Mautern.jpg/1280px-Graphite_found_near_Mautern.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Graphite_found_near_Mautern.jpg/500px-Graphite_found_near_Mautern.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGraphite_found_near_Mautern.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Graphite_ambient_STM.jpg/120px-Graphite_ambient_STM.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Graphite_ambient_STM.jpg/250px-Graphite_ambient_STM.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Graphite_ambient_STM.jpg/120px-Graphite_ambient_STM.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGraphite_ambient_STM.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Graphite-layers-side-3D-balls.png/120px-Graphite-layers-side-3D-balls.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Graphite-layers-side-3D-balls.png/250px-Graphite-layers-side-3D-balls.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Graphite-layers-side-3D-balls.png/120px-Graphite-layers-side-3D-balls.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_ca